course: dictionary
lesson: 14567
title: Picture words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in your mind. Picturesque is one of them. It describes a place that is so pretty it looks like a picture or a postcard. «The little village had cottages with red roofs and flowers in every window.» The clues are cottages, flowers and windows, which make a pretty scene you can picture, so picturesque fits.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «The little village was picturesque.» Does it still make sense? Yes, because the words around it describe something lovely to look at. Picturesque is usually about how a place looks.
explain: Writers can also use picturesque to describe language. «Her story was picturesque, full of bright colours and busy markets.» Here the writing itself is vivid and colourful, so it paints a clear scene for the reader.
fact: Picturesque is an adjective, so it describes a noun, such as a picturesque village.
fact: The comparative forms are more picturesque and most picturesque.
fact: «Picturesque» means very pretty, like a picture or a postcard, especially an old village or a countryside view.
fact: «Picturesque» can also describe writing or speech that is vivid, colourful and full of interesting description.
fact: Similar words include pretty, scenic and charming, but picturesque suggests a view that looks like a painting.
exercise: «The harbour was picturesque, with little boats bobbing beside painted houses.» What does picturesque mean? | Dirty and dark | *Very pretty, like a picture | Very noisy and crowded | Cold and empty
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to picturesque? | Rude | Heavy | Gloomy | *Scenic
exercise: «Her story was picturesque, full of bright colours and busy markets.» What is picturesque describing in this sentence? | A dog | The weather | *The story's writing | A bus
test: «We visited a picturesque valley with a river running through it.» What kind of place is a picturesque valley? | A dark cave | A busy, noisy city | A place with no trees | *A pretty place that looks like a picture
test: Which sentence uses picturesque correctly? | I picturesque my dinner on the plate. | We picturesque to the shop. | She ran picturesque down the road. | *The picturesque old village sat beside the lake.
exam: Which word means very pretty, like a picture? | Hungry | *Picturesque | Curt | Glum
